      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because 50 mg is well above the usual amlodipine range. The standard adult starting dose is 5 mg daily, the usual range is 2.5 to 10 mg daily, and 10 mg is the labeled maximum. Patients with normal kidney and liver function don't need a dose reduction, but 50 mg is still five times the maximum, and an overdose can cause marked hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema.\n\nCould you confirm the intended dose?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily (typical starting dose)\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily (usual maximum)\n- **50 mg** as written, if you intend it, though I'd want you to confirm this is deliberate\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
